# Rendered by fleet-init from fleet.env. Source on the mac venue.
# Samsung SM-G990B phone (1080x2340, 5.2 GB, Android 16), Lenovo TB520FU tablet
# (1840x2944, 14.9 GB, Android 16), Xiaomi 25028RN03Y phone (720x1640, 2.7 GB,
# Android 15) -- all arm64-v8a. The Samsung stays first, so ANDROID_SERIAL and every
# unqualified run are unchanged.
#
# Claim by serial, not by position, when the device matters:
#   HA26QKR0                        the only Android TABLET form factor -- layout checks
#   9b010059305330363400f1f217fa8c  the LOW-MEMORY profile (2.7 GB) -- anything that
#                                   sizes itself to the device, e.g. the live-runtime
#                                   budget (#153/#230). A `web` page's real cost sits in
#                                   a separate renderer process the app's VmRSS never
#                                   sees, so a budget that is merely survivable at 5 GB
#                                   gets the app killed here. This is the device that
#                                   falsifies such a policy rather than confirming it.
export FLEET_ANDROID_SERIALS="RFCRC0FY4ZJ HA26QKR0 9b010059305330363400f1f217fa8c"
# iPad Air 13-inch (M2) sim, physical iPad Air (4th gen), iPhone 16 Pro sim,
# iPad Air 13-inch (M3) sim (iOS 18.4), iPad Air 11-inch (M2) sim, iPhone 16 Pro sim
# (iOS 18.4) as a SECOND phone: the list had four iPad-class devices and one phone, so
# issue 87 — a check that is about an iPhone's width and cannot substitute an iPad —
# sat in a claim-retry loop while four devices it could not use were free.
# The two extra iPads are here because iPad coverage was the scarce one: with four
# agents in flight, issue 112's run found "the two iPads were claimed by other runs"
# and fell back to the iPhone, which is the wrong form factor for a layout check.
# Order matters: the first is what a run takes when it picks no UDID of its own.
export FLEET_IOS_UDIDS="A42682BF-67BA-48CC-875F-B47E31F191FF 5E8DA01B-5B74-5EFB-B9B1-42E9C4707FAB 40696C9C-F8EE-483F-83FF-AFA89CCC5FE7 60F8C0FE-6BC3-4C1A-831E-9678B8B21F8E B8C06040-12CE-4E8D-B43A-53AE3A7B403C 4D2F2641-B0A3-4B55-BF5C-3166299F579A"
export ANDROID_SERIAL="${FLEET_ANDROID_SERIALS%% *}"
